### 1. List (empty first run) -> 200 { data: [], totalCount: 0 }
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2. Create -> 201 { itemId }
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Stripe Payments",
  "upstream": "https://api.stripe.com/v1/charges",
  "methods": ["GET", "post"],
  "headers": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer ${SECRET.STRIPE_KEY}" }]
}

### 3. Get -> methods ["GET","POST"], slug "stripe-payments", path "/api/proxy/gateway/stripe-payments/*", headers[0].isSecretRef true, upstreamMasked "api.st****.com/***"
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. List -> one item, injectedCredential true, totalCount 1
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Slug collision -> 409 PROXY_SLUG_CONFLICT
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Stripe  Payments!", "upstream": "https://api.stripe.com", "methods": ["GET"] }

### 6. Non-https upstream -> 400 PROXY_VALIDATION with errors.upstream
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Bad", "upstream": "ftp://x", "methods": ["GET"] }

### 7. Update (changed) -> 200; the versions list shows v2 ConfigUpdate
PUT {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "{{proxyId}}",
  "name": "Stripe Payments",
  "upstream": "https://api.stripe.com/v2/charges",
  "methods": ["GET", "POST"],
  "headers": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer ${SECRET.STRIPE_KEY}" }]
}

### 8. Update (verbatim repeat) -> 200 no-op; the versions list still tops out at v2
PUT {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "{{proxyId}}",
  "name": "Stripe Payments",
  "upstream": "https://api.stripe.com/v2/charges",
  "methods": ["GET", "POST"],
  "headers": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer ${SECRET.STRIPE_KEY}" }]
}

### 9. Update state disabled -> 200; the versions list shows v3 Toggle "Proxy disabled"
PATCH {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "enabled": false }

### 10. Change history
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}/versions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Revert to v1 -> 200; Get shows original upstream + enabled true, slug unchanged; the versions list shows v4 Revert "Reverted to v1"
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}/versions/{{versionId}}/revert
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Delete -> 200; the list totalCount 0; the versions list still returns history with a top Delete row
DELETE {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Revert after delete -> 409 PROXY_DELETED
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}/versions/{{versionId}}/revert
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 3 (SPEC3): request logs / metrics / CSV export. Read-only over the
# ProxyExecutions rows the Phase-2 data-plane forwarder writes. Generate some
# traffic through /api/proxy/gateway/<slug>/... first.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 14. Overview tiles -> calls24h / avgLatencyMs / errorRatePct / errorRateIsHigh / credentialRefs / methods / lastCallAtUtc (rolling 24h)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}/overview
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 15. Request logs, filtered + paged -> BaseQueryListResponse; totalCount is the unpaged 24h count for the statusClass
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}/executions?statusClass=5xx&pageSize=25&pageNumber=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 16. Live tail -> only rows strictly newer than afterId; pageNumber ignored; totalCount still the full 24h count
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}/executions?afterId=PASTE_NEWEST_ITEM_ID&pageSize=25
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 17. Bad status class -> 400 PROXY_VALIDATION { errors.statusClass: "Must be one of all, 2xx, 4xx, 5xx." }
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}/executions?statusClass=3xx
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 18. Expanded row -> full detail incl. responseBody (clipped to 64 KB with responseBodyTruncatedForDisplay); unknown/mismatched -> 200 data:null
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}/executions/PASTE_ITEM_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 19. Export CSV -> text/csv; charset=utf-8, BOM, header "Time,Method,Path,Status,LatencyMs,UpstreamHost,Outcome,Error", newest-first, <=50k rows (X-Proxy-Export-Truncated: true when more)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}/executions/export?statusClass=all
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 20. Unknown proxy id (no rows) -> 404 PROXY_NOT_FOUND
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/does-not-exist/overview
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 21. The list now carries additive calls24h per card (0 when no executions in the window); every other field + totalCount unchanged
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 22. Structured history -> each ConfigUpdate row carries `changes[]` (one { field, label, before, after } per edited field); Create/Delete rows have `changes: []`
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}/versions?pageSize=50&pageNumber=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 23. Update touching 2 fields -> one new version whose `changes` has 2 entries (see #22 to confirm)
PUT {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "itemId": "{{proxyId}}", "name": "Renamed Proxy", "upstream": "https://api.stripe.com/v2/charges", "methods": ["GET", "POST"], "headers": [], "query": [] }

### 24. Revert this change -> undoes only the fields version {{versionId}} moved; appends a Revert row; 200
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}/versions/{{versionId}}/revert
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 25. Revert an older version after a field it touched moved again -> 409 PROXY_REVERT_CONFLICT { errors: { "<field>": "This field was changed again by a later version." } }
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}/versions/PASTE_OLDER_VERSION_ID/revert
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 26. Revert a Create / Delete / no-op version -> 400 PROXY_VERSION_NOT_REVERTABLE
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}/versions/PASTE_CREATE_VERSION_ID/revert
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase D-feature (PROXY-PLAN-per-method-feature.md): per-method overrides.
# `methodConfigs[]` on Create / Update / Test-draft. A null member inherits the
# shared value; an empty list / blank upstream collapses to inherit; an entry
# whose 3 members are all inherit is dropped. Diff/revert use method-scoped
# addresses `method:<M>:upstream | header:<key> | query:<key>`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 27. Update adding a POST override (different upstream + one header) -> 200; the versions list (#22) shows a row whose `changes` carry `method:POST:upstream` and `method:POST:header:X-Trace`
PUT {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "{{proxyId}}",
  "name": "Stripe Payments",
  "upstream": "https://api.stripe.com/v2/charges",
  "methods": ["GET", "POST"],
  "headers": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer ${SECRET.STRIPE_KEY}" }],
  "methodConfigs": [
    { "method": "POST", "upstream": "https://api.stripe.com/v3/charges", "headers": [{ "key": "X-Trace", "value": "on" }] }
  ]
}

### 28. Get -> `methodConfigs` echoes the POST override; the shared config is unchanged
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 29. Override for a method not in `methods` -> 400 PROXY_VALIDATION { errors.methodConfigs }
PUT {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "{{proxyId}}",
  "name": "Stripe Payments",
  "upstream": "https://api.stripe.com/v2/charges",
  "methods": ["GET"],
  "headers": [],
  "methodConfigs": [{ "method": "POST", "upstream": "https://api.stripe.com/v3/charges" }]
}

### 30. Update removing the override -> 200; the versions list shows a row with `method:POST:upstream` (before set, after null) and `method:POST:header:X-Trace` (removed)
PUT {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "{{proxyId}}",
  "name": "Stripe Payments",
  "upstream": "https://api.stripe.com/v2/charges",
  "methods": ["GET", "POST"],
  "headers": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer ${SECRET.STRIPE_KEY}" }],
  "methodConfigs": []
}

### 31. Revert the removal from #30 -> 200; the POST override is restored
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}/versions/PASTE_VERSION_ID_FROM_30/revert
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 32. Change the override again, then Revert the older (#27) row -> 409 PROXY_REVERT_CONFLICT { errors: { "method:POST:upstream": "..." } }
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}/versions/PASTE_VERSION_ID_FROM_27/revert
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 33. Test an unsaved draft with a per-method override -> 200; the forward uses the POST override's upstream
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/test
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "draft": {
    "upstream": "https://api.stripe.com/v1/charges",
    "methods": ["GET", "POST"],
    "methodConfigs": [{ "method": "POST", "upstream": "https://api.stripe.com/v3/charges" }]
  },
  "method": "POST"
}

###############################################################################
# Request-body merge (BodyMerge) — server-side JSON body injection
###############################################################################

### 34. Create a merge-demo proxy (POST only, one plain + one secret-ref body field) -> 201 { itemId }
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Merge Demo",
  "upstream": "https://httpbin.org/anything",
  "methods": ["POST"],
  "headers": [],
  "bodyMerge": [
    { "key": "account", "value": "acct_123" },
    { "key": "api_key", "value": "${SECRET.DEMO_KEY}" }
  ]
}

### 35. Get -> `bodyMerge` echoes both rows; bodyMerge[1].isSecretRef == true
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 36. Test POST with a JSON object body -> 200; forwarded body is {"amount":10,"account":"acct_123","api_key":"<resolved>"}
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/test
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "proxyId": "{{proxyId}}",
  "method": "POST",
  "body": "{\"amount\":10}",
  "contentType": "application/json"
}

### 37. Test POST with a top-level array body -> 422 RequestBodyNotMergeable, no upstream call
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/test
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "proxyId": "{{proxyId}}",
  "method": "POST",
  "body": "[1,2,3]",
  "contentType": "application/json"
}

### 38. Test POST with an empty body -> 200; forwarded body is {"account":"acct_123","api_key":"<resolved>"}
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/test
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "proxyId": "{{proxyId}}",
  "method": "POST"
}

### 39. Update adding a third body field -> 200; the versions list shows a `body:currency` change pair (before null, after set)
PUT {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "{{proxyId}}",
  "name": "Merge Demo",
  "upstream": "https://httpbin.org/anything",
  "methods": ["POST"],
  "headers": [],
  "bodyMerge": [
    { "key": "account", "value": "acct_123" },
    { "key": "api_key", "value": "${SECRET.DEMO_KEY}" },
    { "key": "currency", "value": "usd" }
  ]
}

### 40. Revert the add from #39 -> 200; the `currency` body field is gone again
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}/versions/PASTE_VERSION_ID_FROM_39/revert
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 41. Create with duplicate body field keys -> 400 PROXY_VALIDATION { errors.bodyMerge: "Each body field key must be unique." }
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Merge Dup",
  "upstream": "https://httpbin.org/anything",
  "methods": ["POST"],
  "bodyMerge": [
    { "key": "account", "value": "a" },
    { "key": "account", "value": "b" }
  ]
}

###############################################################################
# Configuration variables ({{$VAR.name}}) — resolved server-side from Blocks
# Secrets on the forward / Test path only. The stored value keeps the verbatim
# token; the resolved value is never persisted, logged, or returned.
# Needs KeyVault__KeyVaultUrl (+ optionally KeyVault__ClientId / ClientSecret /
# TenantId) configured for the host running the forward — bad credentials
# surface on the first forward that resolves a variable, not at startup.
# Pre-create a `service`- or `both`-typed secret named `stripe-key` first.
###############################################################################

### 42. Create a proxy whose Authorization header references a variable -> 201 { itemId }
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Var Demo",
  "upstream": "https://httpbin.org/anything",
  "methods": ["GET"],
  "headers": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{$VAR.stripe-key}}" }]
}

### 43. Get -> headers[0].value is the verbatim "Bearer {{$VAR.stripe-key}}" (no isSecretRef field); GetOverview.credentialRefs lists "{{$VAR.stripe-key}}"
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 44. Test the proxy -> 200; the upstream (httpbin) echoes header "Authorization: Bearer <resolved value>", and the response body / execution row never contain that value
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/test
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "proxyId": "{{proxyId}}", "method": "GET" }

### 45. Test a draft that references an unknown variable -> 502 { code: "PROXY_GATEWAY_VARIABLERESOLUTIONFAILED" }, no upstream call
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/test
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "draft": {
    "upstream": "https://httpbin.org/anything",
    "methods": ["GET"],
    "headers": [{ "key": "X-Api-Key", "value": "{{$VAR.does-not-exist}}" }]
  },
  "method": "GET"
}

###############################################################################
# Response field filtering (ResponseMode: "All" | "Select")
# Under "Select" the gateway projects the upstream JSON body to responseInclude
# (a structural subset — no rename / hoist / compute). Fail-closed: a non-2xx /
# non-JSON / unparseable / >5 MB upstream fails the call with
# 502 PROXY_GATEWAY_RESPONSEFILTERFAILED and relays nothing. A 2xx JSON
# primitive / array-of-primitives is relayed whole (WholePrimitive).
###############################################################################

### 46. Create a Select proxy that keeps only two fields -> 201 { itemId }
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Resp Filter Demo",
  "upstream": "https://httpbin.org/anything",
  "methods": ["GET"],
  "responseMode": "Select",
  "responseInclude": ["data.id", "data.items[].sku"]
}

### 47. Get -> responseMode "Select", responseInclude ["data.id","data.items[].sku"]
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 48. Test -> 200; response body is the trimmed subset; responseFilterApplied true, responseFilterNote "Applied"
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/test
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "proxyId": "{{proxyId}}", "method": "GET" }

### 49. Update to an empty include list -> 200; a live/Test call now relays {} (responseFilterNote "EmptyResult")
PUT {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/{{proxyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "{{proxyId}}",
  "name": "Resp Filter Demo",
  "upstream": "https://httpbin.org/anything",
  "methods": ["GET"],
  "responseMode": "Select",
  "responseInclude": []
}

### 50. Test a Select draft against a primitive 2xx JSON body -> 200, body relayed whole, responseFilterNote "WholePrimitive"
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/test
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "draft": {
    "upstream": "https://httpbin.org/uuid",
    "methods": ["GET"],
    "responseMode": "Select",
    "responseInclude": ["anything"]
  },
  "method": "GET"
}

### 51. Test a Select draft against an upstream 503 -> 502 { code: "PROXY_GATEWAY_RESPONSEFILTERFAILED", upstreamStatusCode: 503 }
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/test
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "draft": {
    "upstream": "https://httpbin.org/status/503",
    "methods": ["GET"],
    "responseMode": "Select",
    "responseInclude": ["data.id"]
  },
  "method": "GET"
}

### 52. Test a Select draft against a text/html 2xx -> 502 PROXY_GATEWAY_RESPONSEFILTERFAILED ("...was not JSON (text/html)")
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies/test
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "draft": {
    "upstream": "https://httpbin.org/html",
    "methods": ["GET"],
    "responseMode": "Select",
    "responseInclude": ["data.id"]
  },
  "method": "GET"
}

### 53. Create with an invalid field path -> 400 PROXY_VALIDATION { errors.responseInclude: "'items[0]' is not a valid field path." }
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/Proxies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Resp Filter Bad Path",
  "upstream": "https://httpbin.org/anything",
  "methods": ["GET"],
  "responseMode": "Select",
  "responseInclude": ["items[0]"]
}
